    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Suppose that $x$ satisfies both $3x-1<2$ and $2x+3<7$. Solve for $x$, showing your answer on a number line.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x<1$.\n\nBoth inequalities must hold, so take their common solution.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x-1&<2\\\\3x&<3\\\\x&<1\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+3&<7\\\\2x&<4\\\\x&<2\\end{align*}$$\nBoth inequalities hold when $x<1$. The open endpoint excludes $1$.",
